; min-release-age IS a real npm key, and it is version-gated.
;
; Answered from npm's own documentation rather than from CLI behaviour, because
; the CLI cannot answer it: npm 10.9.4 accepts and echoes back a key invented
; for the test, with no warning, so `npm config get` cannot tell an implemented
; key from an ignored one.
;
;   npm v11 documents it: "only versions that were available more than the given
;   number of days ago will be installed" — https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v11/using-npm/config
;   (v11 also adds min-release-age-exclude). The v10 page lists neither.
;
; CI pins node 24, which ships npm 11.x, so this file IS in force there.
; A contributor on npm 10 gets it silently ignored — that is the residual risk,
; and it is why Dependabot carries its own `cooldown: 7` rather than relying on
; this file. See .github/dependabot.yml.

save-exact=true
ignore-scripts=true
min-release-age=7
audit-level=moderate
